{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535011-glorious-solar-saber-fiction","id":535011,"title":"Glorious Solar Saber (Fiction)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-31T19:16:56-07:00","id":535011,"title":"Glorious Solar Saber (Fiction)","content":"It was the height of the First Age, and a young Solar knelt at the feet of her Sifu, a Sidereal master of the ancient arts of war. &quot;Master.&quot; She said, bowing her head in respect, &quot;Teach me how to harness these strange powers that the Most High grants me.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Sifu smacked the Solar upside the head with his cane.<br /> <br /> &quot;You have no powers.&quot; She barked, his wrinkled face frowning at his student. &quot;You are no sorcerer! You cast no spells or weave no workings. Your might is inspired <i>by</i> the Unconquered Sun, not <i>from</i> Him!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But master, I have seen my brothers and sisters do wondrous things! I have seen them walk in to the Wyld and shape it to their desires, I have seen them cure the sick and wounded with but a touch, or move so softly they defy perception! How can these not be the powers of the Unconquered Sun?&quot; She demanded.<br /> <br /> The Sifu smacked the Solar upside the head with his cane.<br /> <br /> &quot;They do these things because they have skills you do not, talents you do not. But these are things you can learn.&quot; He said. The Sifu motioned to the spear at the Solar's side. A simple thing, made of polished wood with a steel head. &quot;Your weapon?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Solar nodded, picking up the weapon and offering it to her Sifu. &quot;Yes master, it was with me the day I was blessed by the Unconquered Sun, when I defeated the Hundred Tiger in single combat. It has been with me ever since that day.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A mighty deed, how long has that been since that day?&quot; Asked the Sifu, a twinkle in his eye.<br /> <br /> &quot;Over a month.&quot; Said the Solar.<br /> <br /> &quot;But you've used this weapon for much longer than that, haven't you?&quot; Asked the Sifu.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes master.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;How long?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Since I was a girl, practicing to become a guardsman for my town with my father.&quot; She said<br /> <br /> The Sifu's face now held a knowing smile. &quot;And how do you feel, with your weapon in my hand?&quot; He asked.<br /> <br /> &quot;Lacking.&quot; Said the Solar, her eyes on the spear in her master's hand. 'Like I'm missing a piece of myself.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Stand and close your eyes.&quot; Said the Sifu. &quot;Do not open them until I command you.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Solar stood, her eyes lingering on her weapon for a moment before complying.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hold out your hand. I am going to return your spear to you.&quot; Said the Sifu.<br /> <br /> The Solar held out her hand, and a heard the Sifu toss the spear to her. She reached out reflexively felt it's weight in her palm as she grasped it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Describe the spear to me.&quot; Said the Sifu.<br /> <br /> With her eyes still closed, the Solar ran her fingers across the blade of the spear and down the body of the weapon. &quot;It's heavier than a normal spear, off balance towards the bottom of the shaft where I had to cut off the tip where it was recently damaged. I haven't had time to fully repair it. Near the top there is a small nick where I struck aside the Hundred Tiger's blow and moved in for the kill. The center is worn down from use, but the feathers at the base of the blade are still soft.&quot; She said.<br /> <br /> &quot;Open your eyes.&quot; Commanded the Sifu.<br /> <br /> The Solar complied once more, and her mouth fell open in amazement. In her hand was not her spear, her treasured battle companion, but instead a glowing shaft of light, thrumming with power beyond mortal imaginings. The noonday light perfectly mimicked the weapon she thought she had held, it even held sparkles of sun-dust in the shape of feathers towards the top.<br /> <br /> &quot;How is this possible?&quot; Asked the Solar, looking at her Sifu and seeing that he still held her true spear.<br /> <br /> &quot;You have carried your weapon for so long, used it so frequently, that it's become a part of who you are.&quot; Said the Sifu, this time truly handing her back her weapon. The Solar accepted it gratefully in her other hand, and marveled at how alike they were. &quot;Because it is a part of you, it can never be truly taken from you. When your soul reached out for a weapon that was not there, your hand answered and granted you a weapon that it knew you could wield.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Amazing.&quot; Said the Solar. &quot;I did not know that the Unconquered Sun could do such things for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Sifu sighed, and smacked the Solar upside the head with his cane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 06-01-2015, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T20:34:45-07:00","id":535153,"title":"","content":"I'm not certain what you mean? He's asking her how she feels about the fact that he has her weapon and she doesn't.<br /> <br /> I'm glad you enjoyed it, though!<br /> <br /> EDIT: And the post I was replying to disappeared. Weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 05-31-2015, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T20:50:21-07:00","id":535159,"title":"","content":"Nice work on the story! I wonder if the Solar is just really faithful or the Sifu has possibly given her enough head trauma with that cane to lead to short term memory loss while she's been training with him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6208-nevanchel","name":"Nevanchel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T20:58:08-07:00","id":535160,"title":"","content":"I like to imagine that it's more the former than the latter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T20:59:04-07:00","id":535162,"title":"","content":"Silly Solar, your power is OF the sun, not FROM the sun!<br /> <br /> ...or is it the other way around? I always get that mixed up...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T23:02:36-07:00","id":535266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535011-glorious-solar-saber-fiction?p=535162#post535162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silly Solar, your power is OF the sun, not FROM the sun!</div> </div> </div> </div>The key thing is that it's actually both at once.<br /> <br /> The fun part for this Sifu won't be getting this Solar to realize that the power comes from his own awesometudinous abilities and is merely facilitated by the Exaltation. It will be getting him to realize that it isn't a binary choice between that and having cool powers you fire off by running Essence through them; both things can be happening at the <i>same time</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T23:23:09-07:00","id":535281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535011-glorious-solar-saber-fiction?p=535266#post535266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The key thing is that it's actually both at once.<br /> <br /> The fun part for this Sifu won't be getting this Solar to realize that the power comes from <b>his</b> own awesometudinous abilities and is merely facilitated by the Exaltation. It will be getting him to realize that it isn't a binary choice between that and having cool powers you fire off by running Essence through them; both things can be happening at the <i>same time</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar's a lady! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T06:18:19-07:00","id":535508,"title":"","content":"Was this in reply to our conversation? That's an awesome piece to just write up all of a sudden. Loved it!<br /> <br /> I don't even really know what to compliment specifically since the entire thing was so well written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T07:32:50-07:00","id":535572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535011-glorious-solar-saber-fiction?p=535281#post535281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Solar's a lady! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lies.<br /> <br /> Or I made a mistake.<br /> <br /> One of the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T09:01:31-07:00","id":535659,"title":"","content":"@Childofthesun: Not specifically, I just noticed that I had been talking about how charms aren't spells more frequently recently, and since Glorious Solar Saber was a charm most often pointed out as being &quot;magic&quot; rather than an expression of skill, I decided to write the story about that charm.<br /> <br /> In my mind, Glorious Solar Saber and the similar charms like stem from a specific tactical illusion that people experience after wearing or carrying a certain object for prolonged periods of time. For example, if I wear a watch all day, every day for a week, but then one day I go out to run errands and forget it, I feel like I'm missing something.<br /> <br /> For a Solar, this sensation is most common with weapons and armor that they've trained with extensively, as those are their most important items in the Age of Sorrows. They see themselves in their mind's eye with their preferred weapon, and they know their weapon and how to use it so well they could describe it to you in great detail while blindfolded. When they lack their preferred weapon but have a desire for it, their Solar nature allows them to rise to the challenge of being unarmed, with their Anima hardening in to a shape that they know how to wield intimately. Thus, Glorious Solar Saber, Immaculate Golden Bow, Glorious Solar Plate, or Fiery Solar Chakram.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 06-01-2015, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T09:55:15-07:00","id":535689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535011-glorious-solar-saber-fiction?p=535659#post535659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Childofthesun: Not specifically, I just noticed that I had been talking about how charms aren't spells more frequently recently, and since Glorious Solar Saber was a charm most often pointed out as being &quot;magic&quot; rather than an expression of skill, I decided to write the story about that charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that thread. There was a lot of resolutely binary thinking in it.<br /> <br /> I harp on it a lot because it's important to me, but I get somewhat irked when a choice is presented between either &quot;everything a Solar does is an expression of their skill, Charms don't actually exist&quot; or &quot;Charms are discrete Essence techniques that are functionally indistinguishable from a magic spell; you deposit Essence and it generates an effect.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because you don't have to choose. For most Solars, the answer is explicitly going to be &quot;both are true.&quot; Glorious Solar Saber for most Solars is going to be precisely how JayTee describes it... but it's still going to be magic; they still need Essence and an Exaltation to rise to the challenge of not having their preferred weapon.<br /> <br /> There's also probably going to be a spectrum involved for some Charms. There are going to be cool-headed savant Solars who had never strapped on a piece of armor in their lives before learning how to invoke Glorious Solar Plate, and who learnt the Charm the way they'd learn a Martial Arts Charm. They think of it explicitly as a Charm they make a conscious effort to use and can explain it in detail and probably train others in its use in a formal way. For them, it's magic first, skill second.<br /> <br /> There is also gonna be that guy who simply manifests Glorious Solar Plate around himself every time he runs screaming in a berserker rage at a Legion, swinging his daiklave in great foe-cutting arcs. He might not even be aware of what he's doing, he certainly doesn't think of it as a Charm as opposed to something that just happens when it needs to, and asking him to teach it to you will get you puzzled looks from him. For him, it's skill first, magic second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 06-01-2015, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T11:33:08-07:00","id":535749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535011-glorious-solar-saber-fiction?p=535689#post535689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember that thread. There was a lot of resolutely binary thinking in it.<br /> <br /> I harp on it a lot because it's important to me, but I get somewhat irked when a choice is presented between either &amp;quot;everything a Solar does is an expression of their skill, Charms don't actually exist&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Charms are discrete Essence techniques that are functionally indistinguishable from a magic spell; you deposit Essence and it generates an effect.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Because you don't have to choose. For most Solars, the answer is explicitly going to be &amp;quot;both are true.&amp;quot; Glorious Solar Saber for most Solars is going to be precisely how JayTee describes it... but it's still going to be magic; they still need Essence and an Exaltation to rise to the challenge of not having their preferred weapon.<br /> <br /> There's also probably going to be a spectrum involved for some Charms. There are going to be cool-headed savant Solars who had never strapped on a piece of armor in their lives before learning how to invoke Glorious Solar Plate, and who learnt the Charm the way they'd learn a Martial Arts Charm. They think of it explicitly as a Charm they make a conscious effort to use and can explain it in detail and probably train others in its use in a formal way. For them, it's magic first, skill second.<br /> <br /> There is also gonna be that guy who simply manifests Glorious Solar Plate around himself every time he runs screaming in a berserker rage at a Legion, swinging his daiklave in great foe-cutting arcs. He might not even be aware of what he's doing, he certainly doesn't think of it as a Charm as opposed to something that just happens when it needs to, and asking him to teach it to you will get you puzzled looks from him. For him, it's skill first, magic second.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's funny to say it's binary, because I've been insisting that Charms are all magical techniques that are explicitly not spells, not widgets to be turned on and off, and a lot of people use their charms subconsciously, not thinking of them as techniques at all. But they still are, in the the same way a right straight or threading a needle are techniques.<br /> <br /> So exactly what you said, except approached from the technique side. Charms exist, are techniques, but are not spells. Option c, thanks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, JayTee, I like your reasoning for the equipment charms. That's pretty cool. Not sure that would be my default, since you can make weapons that you don't own, but really cool for certain characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T15:02:55-07:00","id":535980,"title":"","content":"Hate to deflate your fun-balloon, but I have a small number of nitpicks.<br /> <br /> For one, you keep using &quot;apart&quot; when context suggests you mean &quot;a part.&quot;<br /> <br /> Second, GSS and its equivalents don't just summon a sword or armor - it's <i>an artifact</i>. Your spear won't resemble a wood-and-steel weapon, it is a shaft of molten sunlight, an orichalcum dire lance. Perhaps if your bond is with one mundane weapon in particular it might look like an idealized artifact version of such, cast in glorious sun-metal, but at minimum that means it's probably quite a bit bigger.<br /> <br /> Third, barring some Ship of Theseus type replacement, I doubt an ordinary mortal's spear is going to last that long if she's seeing combat anywhere close to regularly for years and years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T15:42:53-07:00","id":536021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535011-glorious-solar-saber-fiction?p=535980#post535980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one, you keep using &quot;apart&quot; when context suggests you mean &quot;a part.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for catching that. Fixed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535011-glorious-solar-saber-fiction?p=535980#post535980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, GSS and its equivalents don't just summon a sword or armor - it's <i>an artifact</i>. Your spear won't resemble a wood-and-steel weapon, it is a shaft of molten sunlight, an orichalcum dire lance. Perhaps if your bond is with one mundane weapon in particular it might look like an idealized artifact version of such, cast in glorious sun-metal, but at minimum that means it's probably quite a bit bigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, although perhaps not the point of the story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535011-glorious-solar-saber-fiction?p=535980#post535980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, barring some Ship of Theseus type replacement, I doubt an ordinary mortal's spear is going to last that long if she's seeing combat anywhere close to regularly for years and years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also fair, but having your signature weapon break is totally lame and uncool, so it's not likely to actually happen in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T15:59:05-07:00","id":536033,"title":"","content":"You misspelled height as &quot;hight&quot; in the first paragraph, but that's sorta missing the point. I think artifacts should come in all shapes and sizes, not just &quot;immense&quot;. An arming sword and short daiklave are nearly identical in proportions. It easily could have been a &quot;light&quot; dire lance.<br /> <br /> Besides that, broken arms can be repaired. Sure, eventually you replace the shaft and head and run into the &quot;this is my great-great grandfather's ax&quot; thing but that's cool!<br /> <br /> Still totally okay with this fiction on all fronts. Play devil's advocate a little less hard Alucard. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T16:00:36-07:00","id":536034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535011-glorious-solar-saber-fiction?p=536021#post536021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also fair, but having your signature weapon break is totally lame and uncool, so it's not likely to actually happen in practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, depends.<br /> <br /> The spear a Solar wielded since before they drew the Second Breath, a weapon they held in hand as the Sun gave them his blessing, and then wielded afterwords through many battles that is broken because its mortal nature could not withstand its Exalted Wielder's divine strength nor that of the foes she pit it against would make for a <i>really</i> boss Exotic Ingredient for an Artifact Weapon.<br /> <br /> Plus, there's a neat symmetry there that I like. The mortal hero is given divine strength and risen up into the Exalted Host, the mortal spear is reforged, alloyed with orichalcum and remade into a divine weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T16:05:25-07:00","id":536036,"title":"","content":"I admit, I'm making some assumptions based on what we know about artifacts in 3e, about how they're rare, impressive and highly sought after. Under those guidelines, I feel confidant in saying that mundane weapons can potentially last you your entire Exalted career.<br /> <br /> I agree entirely about how reforging your favorite mortal weapon in to a godly weapon after it breaks is super cool, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 06-02-2015, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T18:44:08-07:00","id":536356,"title":"","content":"Gonna disagree with you both from play experience and from the fiction that Exalted draws on for inspiration: a number of Charms, spells, and artifacts destroy mundane weapons, from Octavian's Equitable Resolution destroying any mundane weapon that parries it, to Abyssals' Broken Toys Riposte, to Earth Dragon Style and DB Craft Charms\u2026 heck, I'm not a gambling man, but I'd bet the number of Exalt types that have at least one native Charm to fuck up your non-artifact weapon is greater than the number of Exalt types that don't, and I'm not even gonna count Solars' Heavenly Guardian Defense in that spread! <br /> <br /> You know who was an awesome pulp-style adventurer who didn't rely on an artifact weaponry? <b>Conan</b>, fuck yeah. His weapons tend to take a lot of abuse; the combination of the strength of his attacks (often when delivering a stroke he ends up splitting his victim's skull to the teeth, and sometimes shears all the way down to the breastbone) and his tendency to fight tough fights (the opponent is armored, or supernaturally resilient, or as skilled a swordsman as he) tends to result in some pretty bad damage to his weapons. They're often described as heavily-notched or otherwise suffering from some integrity problems; hell, in <i>The Phoenix on the Sword</i>, the titular sword shivers to bits after he smashes it on someone's helmet, and he fights the rest of his mortal opponents with an axe. Oftentimes he loses or is relieved of a weapon, and he never bothers retrieving it - the entirety of <i>Rogues in the House</i> takes place after Conan was jailed, and the whole time his only proper weapon is a knife he takes off his jailer's corpse (though at times in the story he fights with other things, including a joint of beef, and once, a stool); he leaves town after that, so whatever weapon he used prior to his imprisonment is left behind.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying everyone should be like Conan. That's not the point of this post. But weapons break. Fighting with one puts it under a <i>lot</i> of stress. It's one thing to imbue an object with sentimental value, and another thing entirely to expect to finish out a decades-long military career with the same weapon you started with intact at the end of it.<br /> <br /> Have a primary weapon, that's fine. But you're smart to carry a spare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-02-2015, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T18:48:37-07:00","id":536361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535011-glorious-solar-saber-fiction?p=536356#post536356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying everyone should be like Conan. That's not the point of this post. But weapons break. Fighting with one puts it under a <i>lot</i> of stress. It's one thing to imbue an object with sentimental value, and another thing entirely to expect to finish out a decades-long military career with the same weapon you started with intact at the end of it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe a Melee(or whatever Ability is appropriate) Charm that allows you to commit Motes to a single mundane weapon in order to grant it Artifact-like resilience(and nothing else, of course)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T20:58:34-07:00","id":536447,"title":"","content":"...Did everyone miss my post? So the weapons broken. Who cares? Just fix it!<br /> <br /> That's an incredibly common trope, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T23:06:51-07:00","id":536559,"title":"","content":"We saw your post. In fact I anticipated it all the way back in the first post I made to the thread. That's why I said &quot;barring some Ship of Theseus type replacement.&quot; You don't <i>fix</i> a broken shaft - you replace it. Eventually the head's going to chip or break or bend or get sharpened down to a sliver, or snap off in an enemy where you can't recover it, and then you have to replace that, too. Like the Ship of Theseus, is it still the same spear after you've replaced every part of it? How about when you've done it ten times? What if you later improve on the design in some way? And so on!<br /> <br /> It's a can of worms and just getting <i>two</i> people to agree on any given position has been pretty difficult in the past. Which is why I was skipping right over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-02-2015, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T23:41:40-07:00","id":536638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535011-glorious-solar-saber-fiction?p=535980#post535980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, GSS and its equivalents don't just summon a sword or armor - it's <i>an artifact</i>. Your spear won't resemble a wood-and-steel weapon, it is a shaft of molten sunlight, an orichalcum dire lance. Perhaps if your bond is with one mundane weapon in particular it might look like an idealized artifact version of such, cast in glorious sun-metal, but at minimum that means it's probably quite a bit bigger.<br /> <br /> Third, barring some Ship of Theseus type replacement, I doubt an ordinary mortal's spear is going to last that long if she's seeing combat anywhere close to regularly for years and years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to take the opposite point of view here. <br /> <br /> GSS makes artifacts sure, but who says the artifact has to be huge. They typically are, that is the style of the game, but I don't see it as a requirement. Given the backstory here, I think it is very appropriate for the GSS to manifest as a duplicate of her well-known spear. With use, she may find that her new GSS is far more effective than her old weapon ever was though (it has artifact stats despite its appearance)<br /> <br /> The Solar in the story has only been exalted for a month. She may have been in a large number of battles but most likely few were against supernatural foes. In fact the only really powerful supernatural foe she has faced at this point may have been the one she exalted against. A mortal spear could last through any number of fights against mortal or low power enemies, provided it is well maintained and repaired. This is a piece of fiction based on a game, not real life. I think most storytellers would at most require the occasional craft role to repair the weapon. Fun trumps realism when it comes to things like gear maintenance. The story does specifically say the spear has been repaired before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1203-caladon","name":"Caladon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T05:34:06-07:00","id":536854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/535011-glorious-solar-saber-fiction?p=536559#post536559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We saw your post. In fact I anticipated it all the way back in the first post I made to the thread. That's why I said &quot;barring some Ship of Theseus type replacement.&quot; You don't <i>fix</i> a broken shaft - you replace it. Eventually the head's going to chip or break or bend or get sharpened down to a sliver, or snap off in an enemy where you can't recover it, and then you have to replace that, too. Like the Ship of Theseus, is it still the same spear after you've replaced every part of it? How about when you've done it ten times? What if you later improve on the design in some way? And so on!<br /> <br /> It's a can of worms and just getting <i>two</i> people to agree on any given position has been pretty difficult in the past. Which is why I was skipping right over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I've Never been exposed to the Ship of Theseus version of the trope so I didn't know what that meant. Sorry. (Embarrassed)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":4729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","user":"Childofthesun1","date":". 06-02-2015, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}